WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:33.880 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  when the sky roars I climb to the top  [Music]  the sensations ow  cool drops felt against  the chill sends me into a kind of giddy  [Music]  the clouds left  warm rays permeate the canopy  [Music]  muddy river banks black in my paws  fog voices and beads in my hair  [Music]  we call the forest home  [Music]  faint smells guide me on a constant  search for food  I traced the musty odour of a soft log  to termites I didn't always walk the  forest alone I had a mother and brother  once we used to rip open bogs and dig  for earthworms together but one day  mom's foot got stuck in a snare I was  off eating fruit when I heard gunshots  ricochet through the trees I saw my mom  leave the forest and a bag that day and  my brother in a small metal cage the  whirring of bees always reminds me of my  mother  she described honey as being the  treasure of the forest no matter how  high  I'll always climb for it  I'm alone now but there are others  sometimes I try to mock fight with them  like my brother and I used to they don't  understand me though  i pile branches and damp leaves until  the moonlight fills the cup of my nest  my eyes fall to a close on the sand of  peaceful off an unfamiliar racket  interrupts the morning choir an  orangutan sounds his alarm an intruder  [Music]  after weeks the noise finally stopped  but I was replaced with the smell of ash  [Music]  it's the ones who took my mother and  brother  [Music]  away the only place we all call home  [Music]  and replace it with endless rows of  strange trees  [Music]  the forest is too small now fruit is  scarce I am forced to leave or starve  [Music]  but can I live here with all the men and  roads  [Music]  I enter a form of hysteria when my paw  gets stuck in a snare like what happened  to my mother  because this where they took my brother  their new smells here but I can't get  out to find them  the constant itch on my stomach drives  me to insanity  whyever smell the forest again  [Music]  three mother don't do that it was easier  [Music]  the aroma of snake fruit and banana a  sort of silver lining  [Music]  I'm gaining weight and feeling stronger  I can stretch my limbs to climb again  they try to simulate the forest honey  hidden and smooth logs miniature  downpours Li cheese-stuffed and Ryan's  my teeth can't puncture my heart aches  last year but I yearn for the forest  where are they taking me now I awake  under a disorienting prisms like a swarm  of familiar smells sends me into a shock  wild blood rushes through my body  Hanan water  heavy rain  for others  boundless  [Music]  [Applause]  I wonder how long the forest war remains  standing  how long will they let me stay  [Music]  [Laughter]  [Music]

